# Docker build context for the container services.
#
# This lives at the repository root because `apps/api`'s image builds from the
# root context — pnpm keeps one lockfile for the whole workspace and a
# `--frozen-lockfile` install cannot find it from a package-level context.
#
# Everything the image needs is copied explicitly by the Dockerfile, so this
# list exists to keep the context small: without it every rebuild uploads the
# whole monorepo, including four `.next` directories.

# Dependencies and build output — reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
.open-next
**/.open-next
.turbo
**/.turbo
.wrangler
**/.wrangler
coverage
**/coverage

# Python virtualenvs and caches. The remaining FastAPI services keep theirs in
# the tree, and `apps/api/.venv` survives locally after the Express cutover;
# together they are ~700MB of context that no image needs.
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache

# Playwright and test artefacts.
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
test-results
**/test-results

# Generated Prisma clients — regenerated in the image against its own platform.
**/src/lib/db/generated
**/src/db/generated

# Secrets and local environment files.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.dev.vars
!**/.env.example

# Local-only agent state. `.claude/worktrees` holds full checkouts of the repo,
# so leaving it in doubles the context on its own.
.claude/tracker
.claude/worktrees

.git
.github
*.log
